// Outline of Indonesia only (no Malaysia/PNG/Philippines/Timor-Leste), traced
// from Wikimedia Commons "Indonesia blank map colored.svg"
// (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indonesia_blank_map_colored.svg),
// by en:User:Indon / Addicted04, CC BY-SA 3.0 / GFDL 1.2+ — attribution is
// carried here and rendered as a small credit line under the map in
// IndonesiaMap.tsx.
//
// That source colours each Indonesian province a distinct bright colour and
// every neighbouring country a flat neutral grey, specifically so the two can
// be told apart programmatically. Extracted every filled path/polygon EXCEPT
// the grey ones (Sabah/Sarawak on Borneo, PNG on New Guinea, Philippines,
// Timor-Leste — all present in the source file's bounding box) and the
// fill="none" administrative border strokes, then combined the rest into one
// multi-subpath `d`. An earlier attempt used the plain (uncoloured) blank map,
// which has no such distinction and rendered Malaysia/PNG/etc. as if they were
// part of Indonesia — wrong for a "real map" and the reason this file exists
// instead of that first one.
//
// Simplified with svgo (precision 0) afterward: 515 subpaths, ~452KB -> 106KB.
// Native viewBox kept (0 0 1876 861) so hub-marker coordinates in
// IndonesiaMap.tsx can sit at real, roughly-projected city locations.

